[{"category":"section","location":"library/#PoissonSolvers-Library-Functions","page":"Library","text":"","title":"PoissonSolvers Library Functions"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#PoissonSolvers.PoissonSolution","page":"Library","text":"Takes a basis and a coefficient vector and returns an appropriate object  that allows to evaluate the corresponding solution via a functor via\n\nsol = PoissonSolution(basis, coeffs)\nsol(x)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PoissonSolvers.PoissonSolution"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#PoissonSolvers.solve!","page":"Library","text":"Solves the Poisson equation for periodic boundary conditions\n\nfunction solve!(p::PoissonSolver, x::AbstractVector, w::AbstractVector) end\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PoissonSolvers.solve!"},{"category":"section","location":"poisson/#Poisson-Solvers","page":"Overview","text":"Solve\n\n- Delta phi(x) = f(x)\n\nusing Plots\nusing PoissonSolvers\n\nsol(x) = sin(π*x) * (1-x^2)\nder(x) = π * cos(π*x) * (1-x^2) - 2 * x * sin(π*x)\nrhs(x) = 4π * x * cos(π*x) + 2 * sin(π*x) + π^2 * (1-x^2) * sin(π*x)\n\ndomain = (-1., +1.)\n\nx = LinRange(domain[begin], domain[end], 100)","title":"Poisson Solvers"},{"category":"section","location":"poisson/#FFT-Solver","page":"Overview","text":"b = FFTWBasis(domain, 256)\np = Potential(b, rhs)\n\nplot(xlabel = \"x\", ylabel = \"ϕ(x)\")\nplot!(x, p.(x); xlims = domain, label = \"Solution\")\nplot!(x, sol.(x); xlims = domain, label = \"Reference\")\n\nplot(xlabel = \"x\", ylabel = \"ϕ'(x)\")\nplot!(x, p.(x, Derivative(1)); xlims = domain, label = \"Derivative\")\nplot!(x, der.(x); xlims = domain, label = \"Reference\")","title":"FFT Solver"},{"category":"section","location":"poisson/#B-Spline-Solver","page":"Overview","text":"b = PeriodicBasisBSplineKit(domain, 3, 32)\np = Potential(b, rhs)\n\nplot(xlabel = \"x\", ylabel = \"ϕ(x)\")\nplot!(x, p.(x); xlims = domain, label = \"Solution\")\nplot!(x, sol.(x); xlims = domain, label = \"Reference\")\n\nplot(xlabel = \"x\", ylabel = \"ϕ'(x)\")\nplot!(x, p.(x, Derivative(1)); xlims = domain, label = \"Derivative\")\nplot!(x, der.(x); xlims = domain, label = \"Reference\")","title":"B-Spline Solver"},{"category":"section","location":"#PoissonSolvers","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for PoissonSolvers.\n\n","title":"PoissonSolvers"}]
